-> confined to fixtures/application/web (plus domain/Format.java, shared, generic).

$ grep -rl "infrastructure" backend/src/main/java/click/kivvi/web/
(no matches -- web never imports infrastructure directly)

ArchUnit (ArchitectureTest, run above, exit 0) additionally proves for the whole codebase:
  - domain never depends on web
  - infrastructure is only accessed from infrastructure or application (so scheduling can
    only be reached via application, never from web or domain directly)
  - web/application/domain/infrastructure form no package cycle
These three rules jointly enforce "no reverse dependencies" for both the new scheduling code
and the new landing/feeds code; all passed with 0 failures.
